  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper presents a noiseless Qiskit Aer implementation of quantum amplitude estimation for European call pricing on a tokenized Bitcoin asset, using 9 qubits, ~250 gates, and 8,192 shots. Across 3-6 price qubits (8-64 bins), the reported discretization error halves exactly with each qubit increase (49,616 -> 24,808 -> 12,404 -> 6,202 USD), but the quantum estimate remains far less accurate than classical Monte Carlo, which reaches 0.23% relative error with 100,000 samples in 0.0053 s.",
